{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For one of these.</b> Rashi explained: and what does it say? I might think only the severe ones among them, etc. — meaning, for instance, if he ate consecrated food, it would be a ewe or a she-goat; and the lighter ones, for instance if he heard the voice of an oath, it would be a bird; and the lightest of the light, for instance vain utterance of the lips, it would be a tenth of an ephah, etc."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:03.787670702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}